  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Which of the following statements are correct?</p><p>(A) The electronic configuration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>Ar</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math>.</p><p>(B) The magnetic quantum number may have a negative value.</p><p>(C) In the ground state of an atom, the orbitals are filled in order of their increasing energy order.</p><p>(D) The total number of nodes are given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.</p>",
